            <fr:title text="ForesterPad: iPad App Redesign">ForesterPad: iPad App Redesign</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>TODO</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="status">cancelled</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p><html:strong>Retired 2026-04-16.</html:strong> Replaced by Notes/Notability → capture endpoint on macproseph (see <fr:link href="/sss-0088/" title="Forest Sync and Capture Architecture" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-0088/" display-uri="sss-0088" type="local">Forest Sync and Capture Architecture</fr:link>). The custom iPad client isn't worth maintaining when a share-sheet Shortcut into <html:code>/capture</html:code> covers the same ingest flow with a fraction of the code. Existing handwriting trees (<html:code>hwn-*</html:code> and the <html:code>notebook-app=forester-pad</html:code> meta) are preserved as-is.</html:p>
            <html:p>Original design below is kept for historical reference.</html:p>
            <html:p>Redesign ForesterPad from a handwriting-focused notes app into a touch-first forest client. Derived from design notes in <fr:link href="/hwn-0003/" title="Forester Server Design" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/hwn-0003/" display-uri="hwn-0003" type="local">Handwriting <fr:contextual-number uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/hwn-0003/" display-uri="hwn-0003" /></fr:link>.</html:p>
            <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
              <fr:frontmatter>
                <fr:authors>
                  <fr:author>
                    <fr:link href="/stevenschaefer/" title="Steven Schaefer" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/stevenschaefer/" display-uri="stevenschaefer" type="local">Steven Schaefer</fr:link>
                  </fr:author>
                </fr:authors>
                <fr:date>
                  <fr:year>2026</fr:year>
                  <fr:month>2</fr:month>
                  <fr:day>27</fr:day>
                </fr:date>
                <fr:source-path>/Users/stevenschaefer/forest/trees/sss-0072.tree</fr:source-path>
                <fr:title text="Small Fixes">Small Fixes</fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p><html:strong>Bridge treeId sync bug</html:strong>: The server's data directory is missing most notes, so the bridge can't assign treeIds back to the iPad. Debug why only 2 of ~15 notes are in the server's data dir.</html:p>
                <html:p><html:strong>PencilKit toolbar activation</html:strong>: Double-tap eraser doesn't work on note switch. PKToolPicker not becoming active for the new first responder.</html:p>
                <html:p><html:strong>Claude skill for handwritten trees</html:strong>: Define a skill that reads a handwritten tree's PDF and transcribes it.</html:p>
                <html:p><html:strong>Emacs todo keybinding</html:strong>: Elisp function to create a TODO tree and insert a transclusion link at point.</html:p>
              </fr:mainmatter>
            </fr:tree>
            <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
              <fr:frontmatter>
                <fr:authors>
                  <fr:author>
                    <fr:link href="/stevenschaefer/" title="Steven Schaefer" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/stevenschaefer/" display-uri="stevenschaefer" type="local">Steven Schaefer</fr:link>
                  </fr:author>
                </fr:authors>
                <fr:date>
                  <fr:year>2026</fr:year>
                  <fr:month>2</fr:month>
                  <fr:day>27</fr:day>
                </fr:date>
                <fr:source-path>/Users/stevenschaefer/forest/trees/sss-0072.tree</fr:source-path>
                <fr:title text="Medium Changes">Medium Changes</fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p><html:strong>Apple Vision OCR</html:strong>: Run VNRecognizeTextRequest on-device after save, store OCR text, bridge writes <![CDATA[\meta{ocr-text}]]> to the tree file. Enables full-text search of handwritten notes.</html:p>
                <html:p><html:strong>Flexible metadata/taxonomy</html:strong>: Remove hardcoded Handwriting taxon. Add a metadata editor panel in the app. Handwritten-ness should be a tag, not a taxon. Trees routing to PDFs should support arbitrary metadata, digital text, and mixed content.</html:p>
                <html:p><html:strong>Custom toolbar actions</html:strong>: Overlay forest-specific buttons alongside PencilKit toolbar (create todo, insert transclusion, set taxon). Equivalent to Emacs forest functions but for touch.</html:p>
              </fr:mainmatter>
            </fr:tree>
            <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
              <fr:frontmatter>
                <fr:authors>
                  <fr:author>
                    <fr:link href="/stevenschaefer/" title="Steven Schaefer" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/stevenschaefer/" display-uri="stevenschaefer" type="local">Steven Schaefer</fr:link>
                  </fr:author>
                </fr:authors>
                <fr:date>
                  <fr:year>2026</fr:year>
                  <fr:month>2</fr:month>
                  <fr:day>27</fr:day>
                </fr:date>
                <fr:source-path>/Users/stevenschaefer/forest/trees/sss-0072.tree</fr:source-path>
                <fr:title text="Large Architectural Changes">Large Architectural Changes</fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p><html:strong>Full forest on iPad</html:strong>: The app should maintain a local copy of the entire forest, not just handwritten notes. Treat iPad and laptop uniformly. Bidirectional sync of all trees.</html:p>
                <html:p><html:strong>Canvas as element, not note</html:strong>: A handwritten canvas should be an element within a tree, not the entirety of it. Trees can mix canvas regions with digital text, transclusions, and queries.</html:p>
                <html:p><html:strong>Forest-as-notebook UI</html:strong>: Replace the flat note list with a rendered, navigable forest. Swipe for forward/back, touch-first interaction, inline canvas editing, visible metadata panel, context and backlinks accessible from within the app.</html:p>
              </fr:mainmatter>
            </fr:tree>
